      ":question/worked-solution": "Notice that we are given an equation of the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(x,y).\n$$\n\nThe right-hand side is a function of $x$ and $y.$ This means that the slope field varies with both $x$ and $y.$\n\nOf the given slope fields, we note the following slope field does not vary with $x$ given a fixed value of $y.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/generate/repairs/2026-10-20-early-cohort/jobs/17592186172040/review-1-policy-2-e0ceec0efc26ec01/assets/17592186172040/plots/2cb6b5c7f2df2f7305d8d1093b3bf03499179a31dc2d3840594f15516dd9a8b9.png)\n\n \n\nTo see this more clearly, notice that if we draw a horizontal line, the slopes do not vary.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/generate/repairs/2026-10-20-early-cohort/jobs/17592186172040/review-1-policy-2-e0ceec0efc26ec01/assets/17592186172040/plots/71c5ba9669354d6fa117973d90e06b0380d12f2f74a572570fe7053b8a8f87f8.png)",
